      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُهُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ طَافَ اَلْفَرِيضَةَ وَ هُوَ عَلَى غَيْرِ طُهْرٍ قَالَ «يَتَوَضَّأُ وَ يُعِيدُ طَوَافَهُ فَإِنْ كَانَ تَطَوُّعاً تَوَضَّأَ وَ صَلَّى رَكْعَتَيْنِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2811 - It is narrated from al-Ala' through Muhammad ibn Muslim from one of the Imams (as)  who said: I asked him about a man who performed the obligatory tawaf without being in a state of purity (wudu).\nImam (as) said: \"He should perform wudu and repeat his tawaf. If it was a voluntary tawaf, he should perform wudu and pray two rak‘ahs.\""
        ]
      }
